## 3. Category Hub Page

The first Category Hub is **Text Tools**, at `/p/text-tools.html`. This page is **not a tool itself** — it's a curated directory of the tools within that category.

**Structure:**

```
Text Tools
│
├── Category Introduction
├── Search / Filter (optional, later)
├── Tool Directory
│   ├── Word Counter
│   ├── Character Counter
│   ├── Case Converter
│   ├── Text Cleaner
│   ├── Sentence Counter
│   ├── Duplicate Line Remover
│   ├── Remove Extra Spaces
│   ├── Line Counter
│   ├── Text Reverser
│   └── ...
├── Related Articles
├── FAQ
└── Footer
```

Ten tools is the right target for the first pass — scale 10 → 20 → 50+ later, matching the Master Spec's 20-to-200+ scaling goal.

**Critical rule, restated from Section 0 correction 4 above and expanded:** in **Phase 1, only Word Counter is real.** The hub page must not list all ten tools with nine dead links pointing at tools that don't exist yet. Two acceptable options:
- List only Word Counter as a real card, and add the rest **only as each one actually publishes**, or
- Show the other nine as visually distinct, unlinked "Coming Soon" labels (no `<a>` tag at all, not even `href="#"`) if you want the directory's eventual shape visible now — this is exactly what Section 14's `published` flag mechanism implements for categories, and the same pattern applies to individual tools within a hub page.

Never a broken or placeholder link in production — this is a hard rule, not a preference.

