## 6. Master Tool Page Template

Every tool Post follows this structure, matching Master Spec Section 8's Standard Tool Page Structure exactly (including the two items — Structured Data and version number — that are easy to forget because they're metadata, not visible content):

```
Tool Post
│
├── Global Header            (from Base_Layout.xml — never duplicated per-post)
├── Breadcrumb
├── H1
├── Tool Introduction
├── Interactive Tool
├── Features
├── How to Use
├── Example
├── Common Use Cases
├── Tips / Best Practices
├── FAQ
├── Related Tools
├── Related Articles
├── Conclusion
├── Last Updated + Version Number
├── Structured Data (JSON-LD — SoftwareApplication, FAQPage, BreadcrumbList)
└── Global Footer            (from Base_Layout.xml — never duplicated per-post)
```

Target: 500–800 words of unique content per tool page (Master Spec Section 8) — this is what separates a real SEO landing page from a bare, thin utility widget.

