## 7. Header & Footer Architecture

**Never rebuild Header/Footer inside a Tool Post.** `Base_Layout.xml`'s theme is the single global owner:

```
Blogger Theme (Base_Layout.xml)
│
├── Global Header
├── Post Content
│   └── Tool Page          ← only this part is post-specific
└── Global Footer
```

The Word Counter post's own HTML should contain **only** what's inside `<b:includable id='post'>` today plus the tool's own interactive UI — never a copy of the header/footer markup. This is already how `Base_Layout.xml` is built (the `post` includable is deliberately minimal), so this section is a confirmation of existing architecture, not a new decision.

Benefits: less duplication, easier maintenance, easier future redesign, consistent branding across every tool — the component-first principle established throughout this project.

