## 14. Publishing a New Tool — Both Registries Must Stay in Sync

**This is a real incident, not a hypothetical.** When Word Counter was created, its URL only got updated in one of the two places that reference tools by URL, leaving the other pointing at a fake `search/label/...` path that was never actually populated — every "Open tool" and every Hero search suggestion for it led to a blank page.

`Base_Layout.xml` has **two separate registries** that must both be updated whenever a tool goes from "planned" to "published" — there is no single source of truth for tool URLs inside the JS today, so this has to be done manually, twice, every time:

| Registry | Location | Powers |
|---|---|---|
| `directory.TOOLS` | `Banynova.register('directory', {...})` | Popular Tools cards, New Tools cards |
| `search.config.popularTools` | `Banynova.register('search', {...})` | Hero search suggestions, rotating placeholder text |

**Checklist for every new tool, no exceptions:**
- [ ] Add the tool to `directory.TOOLS` with its real permalink (e.g. `2026/08/word-counter.html`) — never a `search/label/...` path unless that label genuinely has published posts under it.
- [ ] Add the same tool to `search.config.popularTools` with the same real permalink.
- [ ] Never add a tool to either registry before its Post is actually published and its permalink verified.
- [ ] Run `Testing_Checklist.md` before flipping anything live.

### Category Hub Creation Rule

Formalizing the rule this incident made necessary — each category in `directory.CATEGORIES` carries a `published: true|false` flag:

- **`published: false`** (the default for every category until its hub page is confirmed live) renders as a non-clickable "Coming Soon" card — no `<a href>` at all, so there is no dead link to click.
- **`published: true`** renders as a real link, and must only be set **after** the category's hub page (Section 9's workflow) has been created, published, and its URL verified — never before, and never merely because the page creation *process has started*.
- The homepage/theme may reference a category's intended URL in code before the page exists (as `directory.CATEGORIES` already does for all six categories), but the flag controls whether that reference is ever actually rendered as a clickable link. Code containing an unpublished URL is fine; a live link to one is not.

This is the general pattern — the same `published`-flag-gated rendering should be applied to *any* future homepage element (new tool categories, future Quick Actions, etc.) that references a page or post that might not exist yet at the time the code is written.

